---
import ToolLayout from '../../layouts/ToolLayout.astro';

const faqs = [
  {
    question: "What is the official character limit for a Discord bio?",
    answer: "The strict character limit for a Discord bio (the 'About Me' profile section) is 190 characters. If your text exceeds 190 characters, Discord will prevent you from saving your profile or will abruptly truncate the content."
  },
  {
    question: "Can I use Markdown formatting in my Discord bio?",
    answer: "Yes, Discord bios support standard Markdown formatting. You can use asterisks for bold (**bold**) and italics (*italics*), underscores for underline (__underline__), tildes for strikethrough (~~strikethrough~~), backticks for code (`code`), vertical bars for spoilers (||spoiler||), and standard markdown hyperlinks."
  },
  {
    question: "Do emojis count against the 190-character Discord bio limit?",
    answer: "Yes, all emojis count toward your 190-character budget. Standard Unicode emojis consume 1 to 2 characters. However, custom server emojis consume significantly more space (25 to 35+ characters) because Discord stores their raw code format, such as <:emoji_name:123456789012345678>."
  },
  {
    question: "Can I set different Discord bios for different servers?",
    answer: "Yes, users with an active Discord Nitro subscription can configure 'Server Profiles' (Per-Server Profiles). This allows you to set a professional or tech-focused bio in programming servers while keeping a casual or gaming bio in your community and gaming servers."
  },
  {
    question: "How do I add clickable links to my Discord bio?",
    answer: "You can paste URLs directly (e.g., https://yourlink.com) or use markdown link formatting: [Click Here](https://yourlink.com). To conserve your 190-character budget, use shortened URLs or a unified bio-link tree."
  },
  {
    question: "Why does my Discord bio look broken with custom emojis?",
    answer: "Custom server emojis only render if you share a mutual server where that emoji is hosted, or if you have Discord Nitro allowing global emoji usage. If an emoji is deleted from its host server, it will revert to raw text code."
  },
  {
    question: "What should I include in a gaming Discord bio?",
    answer: "An effective gaming bio should include your main games, preferred in-game roles/agents, competitive rank, time zone or peak active hours, and communication preferences (e.g., 'Mic available for ranked queue')."
  },
  {
    question: "Is this Discord Bio Generator free to use?",
    answer: "Yes, our Discord Bio Generator is 100% free with no account creation or usage limits. You can generate unlimited bio variations across all tones and styles."
  }
];
