        </p>
        <ul>
          <li><code>[system]: online // full-stack dev // building with `Astro` & `TypeScript` 💻</code></li>
          <li><code>netrunner status: code, coffee, and bug fixing. 🤖 | GitHub: cf.gg/dev</code></li>
          <li><code>glitching through cyberspace // backend engineer // terminal native 🌐⚡</code></li>
        </ul>
      </div>

      <div class="step-item">
        <h3>4. Funny, Witty & Sarcastic</h3>
        <p>
          Humorous one-liners designed to make community members laugh when clicking your card.
        </p>
        <ul>
          <li><code>Professionally lazy. Expert in gaming and making terrible life decisions. 🫠</code></li>
          <li><code>My brain has 47 open tabs, and 46 are playing random music. 💀 DM at own risk.</code></li>
          <li><code>I put the 'pro' in procrastination. Sponsoring coffee companies since birth. ☕</code></li>
        </ul>
      </div>

      <div class="step-item">
        <h3>5. Professional, Freelancer & Agency</h3>
        <p>
          Clean, authoritative bios for freelancers, server moderators, and business owners.
        </p>
        <ul>
          <li><code>Product Designer & 3D Artist | Open for freelance commissions 💼 | portfolio: cf.gg</code></li>
          <li><code>Community Director @ CreatorGuild | Inquiries: contact@creatorsfeel.com 🤝</code></li>
          <li><code>Video Editor & Motion Designer // DM for rates & availability // 5+ yrs exp 🎬</code></li>
        </ul>
      </div>

      <div class="step-item">
        <h3>6. Minimalist & Clean</h3>
        <p>
          Sparse, elegant layouts that deliver maximum impact with minimal clutter.
        </p>
        <ul>
          <li><code>music • photography • design | EST time zone | he/him</code></li>
          <li><code>twenty-something • creative soul • chasing sunsets 🌙</code></li>
          <li><code>offline is the new luxury • barista • vinyl collector ☕</code></li>
        </ul>
      </div>

      <div class="step-item">
        <h3>7. Anime & Manga Enthusiast</h3>
        <p>
          Showcase favorite series, character tropes, and Japanese aesthetic symbols.
        </p>
        <ul>
          <li><code>✦ Jujutsu Kaisen & Berserk lover // wandering ronin // 100+ manga read ⚔️</code></li>
          <li><code>living in an anime opening 🌸 | Studio Ghibli soundtrack on repeat 🎧</code></li>
        </ul>
      </div>

      <div class="step-item">
        <h3>8. Content Creator & Streamer</h3>
        <p>
          Drive server traffic directly to your livestreams, YouTube videos, or podcast.
        </p>
        <ul>
          <li><code>🔴 Live on Twitch Tue/Thu @ 7PM EST! | Variety streamer & horror enthusiast 🎮</code></li>
          <li><code>YouTube Creator (50k+) // Talking tech & gear // Watch latest vid: cf.gg/yt 🎬</code></li>
        </ul>
      </div>
    </div>

    <h2>How This Discord Bio Generator Works</h2>
    <p>
      Our generator simplifies bio creation through an automated 4-stage engine:
    </p>
    <ul>
      <li><strong>Keyword Parsing:</strong> Takes your seed interests, favorite games, or job titles and extracts key concepts.</li>
      <li><strong>Tone Synthesis:</strong> Maps your input into curated linguistic structures designed for specific aesthetics (Gaming, Cozy, Cyber, Witty, Professional).</li>
      <li><strong>Decoration Layering:</strong> Optionally weaves Unicode symbols (<code>✦ ✧ ✿</code>), thematic emojis, and markdown links into the copy.</li>
      <li><strong>Character Limit Safety Audit:</strong> Programmatically trims and verifies that every output strictly conforms to the 190-character maximum so it never breaks on Discord.</li>
    </ul>

    <h2>Step-by-Step Guide: How to Use the Tool Effectively</h2>
    <p>
      Follow this simple workflow to update your Discord profile in under two minutes:
    </p>

    <div class="step-guide">
      <div class="step-item">
        <h3>Step 1: Enter Your Keywords or Hobbies</h3>
        <p>
          Type a few terms separated by commas into the <strong>Keywords or Hobbies</strong> field (e.g., <em>'valorant, coffee, web developer'</em> or <em>'reading, tea, graphic design'</em>).
        </p>
      </div>

      <div class="step-item">
        <h3>Step 2: Select Your Bio Tone</h3>
        <p>
          Choose from <strong>Gaming / Competitive</strong>, <strong>Aesthetic / Cozy</strong>, <strong>Cyberpunk / Tech</strong>, <strong>Funny / Witty</strong>, or <strong>Professional / Business</strong>.
        </p>
      </div>

      <div class="step-item">
        <h3>Step 3: Toggle Decorative Enhancements</h3>
        <p>
          Check or uncheck boxes for <strong>Include Emojis</strong>, <strong>Include Sparkles/Decorations</strong>, or <strong>Include Social Link Template</strong> based on your visual preference.
        </p>
      </div>

      <div class="step-item">
        <h3>Step 4: Generate & Preview on the Discord Mockup Card</h3>
        <p>
          Click <strong>Generate Bios</strong> to create a list of custom bios. Click any bio card to instantly preview how it renders inside the dark-mode Discord profile mockup on the right.
        </p>
      </div>

      <div class="step-item">
        <h3>Step 5: Copy & Paste Into Discord</h3>
        <p>
          Click the <strong>Copy Bio</strong> chip button. In your Discord app, navigate to <strong>User Settings ⚙️ $\rightarrow$ Profiles $\rightarrow$ About Me</strong>, paste your bio, and click <strong>Save Changes</strong>.
        </p>
      </div>
    </div>

    <h2>Tips for Writing an Attractive & Unique Discord Bio</h2>
    <p>
      Elevate your Discord presence with these profile design techniques:
    </p>

    <div class="step-guide">
      <div class="step-item">
        <h3>1. Use Vertical Dividers to Organize Information</h3>
        <p>
          Use clean symbols like vertical pipes (<code>|</code>), bullet points (<code>•</code>), slashes (<code>//</code>), or sparkles (<code>✦</code>) to separate hobbies, time zones, and social links. This creates instant scannability on mobile screens.
        </p>
      </div>

      <div class="step-item">
        <h3>2. State Communication & DM Preferences</h3>
        <p>
          Let other server members know how to interact with you (e.g., <em>'DMs open for game invites'</em>, <em>'DMs closed / ping in server'</em>, or <em>'DM for business inquiries only'</em>).
        </p>
      </div>

      <div class="step-item">
        <h3>3. Shorten Long Social URLs</h3>
        <p>
          A long URL like <code>https://instagram.com/yourverylongusername</code> wastes 45+ characters. Use a short custom domain, a link-in-bio service, or clean markdown text: <code>[Instagram](https://yoururl.com)</code>.
        </p>
      </div>

      <div class="step-item">
        <h3>4. Coordinate Banner, Avatar & Bio Palette</h3>
        <p>
          Match your Discord banner color and avatar theme with your bio's emoji palette (e.g., pairing a purple cyberpunk banner with neon emojis like 👾⚡💜).
        </p>
      </div>
    </div>

    <h2>Common Mistakes to Avoid in Discord Bios</h2>
    <p>
      Avoid these common formatting errors that diminish profile appeal:
    </p>

    <div class="callout-box warning">
      <div class="callout-title">
        <span>⚠️</span> Common Profile Pitfalls
      </div>
      <p style="margin: 0; font-size: 0.95rem;">
        Avoid these formatting and design errors to ensure your bio displays cleanly across desktop, tablet, and mobile devices.
      </p>
    </div>

    <ul>
      <li><strong>Exceeding 190 Characters:</strong> Trying to paste text that is too long, resulting in Discord rejecting the save or cutting off crucial contact info.</li>
      <li><strong>Using Unreadable 'Zalgo' or Cursive Fonts:</strong> Using third-party Unicode font generators (e.g., 𝓒𝓾𝓻𝓼𝓲𝓿𝓮) makes your bio illegible on Android devices and completely breaks accessibility for screen readers.</li>
      <li><strong>Unclosed Markdown Formatting Tags:</strong> Forgetting to close bold or italic asterisks (e.g., typing <code>**Developer</code> without the closing <code>**</code>), leaving raw asterisks visible.</li>
      <li><strong>Overfilling with Custom Server Emojis:</strong> If you leave the server where a custom emoji is hosted, the emoji breaks into a raw ID string like <code>&lt;:pepe:849201948291048&gt;</code>.</li>
      <li><strong>Cluttering with Excessive Negative Warnings:</strong> Filling your entire bio with hostile warnings (e.g., <em>'Don't talk to me unless...'</em>) drives away potential friends and gaming partners.</li>
    </ul>

    <h2>How a Great Discord Bio Helps You Stand Out</h2>
    <p>
      A well-crafted Discord bio provides tangible social benefits:
    </p>
    <ol>
      <li><strong>Fast-Track Server Verification:</strong> Many gated gaming and professional communities require staff to review applicant profiles. A complete bio proves you are a genuine human, not a spam bot.</li>
      <li><strong>Effortless Icebreakers:</strong> When community members click your profile, common interests (like shared games or favorite anime) give them an instant conversation starter.</li>
      <li><strong>Inbound Freelance Leads:</strong> In developer and design servers, having a crisp bio showcasing your tech stack and portfolio link routinely generates organic client inquiries.</li>
    </ol>
  </div>
